.DS_Store
.build/
build/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# `.claude/` is ignored whole, not just its two crew links. The crew is
# local: the agent briefs live on disk and are not part of the project's
# history, because they are how one person drives this repository, not
# something it ships. Where `install.sh` has run over a tree, `agents` and
# `crew` under `.claude` are symbolic links into Core Crew for that same
# reason — it creates both under "2. Project trees and their worktrees"
# (`link_dir "$t/.claude/agents" ...` and `link_dir "$t/.claude/crew" ...`),
# and `ls -la .claude` in a checkout it has run against shows the pair
# pointing into Core Crew.
#
# The rest of `.claude/` has to stay out for its own reason: where Claude
# Code has made them, `worktrees/` holds worktree checkouts and
# `settings.local.json` sits beside them as a plain file — nothing in this
# repository creates either. A linked worktree's own `.git` is a text
# pointer at the main tree's `.git/worktrees/<name>`, not a repository of
# its own, but git still treats the directory as one: in a clone carrying
# only this `.gitignore`, `git add -A` without this line would stage
# `settings.local.json` and add a worktree checkout as an embedded git
# repository, with a warning from git itself. `.claude` is itself an
# ordinary directory, so the pattern takes a trailing slash, the same as
# `.build/` and `build/` above and `/.superpowers/` below.
/.claude/

# Only `docs/` stays out of the tree: plans and specs are a record of decisions
# being made, not of what the program is. ARCHITECTURE.md, CLAUDE.md,
# CHANGELOG.md and README.md describe the program itself and belong in the
# repository with it.
/docs

# Brainstorm sessions write HTML mockups here. They are working material for one
# design conversation — the decisions that survive them land in `docs/`, and the
# mockups themselves are worth keeping on disk and out of the history.
/.superpowers/
